{
  "__comment": [
    "THIS FILE IS A TEMPLATE. Rename it to sounds.json to enable the mod's own recordings.",
    "",
    "Yuletide Fireworks ships without .ogg assets on purpose: a convincing firework recording is a",
    "licence and a microphone, not a line of code. The mod is fully playable without this file - the",
    "audio mixer layers vanilla's blast events with distance, air absorption and echo modelling,",
    "which is where most of the perceived quality comes from anyway.",
    "",
    "To use your own audio:",
    "  1. drop the files into  src/main/resources/assets/fireworkshaders/sounds/fireworks/",
    "     (or into a resource pack at the same path),",
    "  2. rename this file to sounds.json in that same assets/fireworkshaders/ folder,",
    "  3. keep 44.1 kHz mono or stereo - the mixer only changes volume, pitch and timing, it does",
    "     not remix, so a mono recording places better in the stereo field.",
    "",
    "Mixer contract, so recordings can be authored against it:",
    "  * boom / boom_far are played at the break, boom_far only for breaks further than 40 blocks,",
    "  * echo is replayed 2-4 times with rising spacing and falling pitch, once per echoCount,",
    "  * crackle is pitched up to 1.6x and volume-scaled per shell, on top of the crackle pops,",
    "  * whistle is a loop-like short sample retriggered during the ascent (pitch rises with height),",
    "  * shriek is used only by the Sonic Boom's SHRIEK lift module,",
    "  * launch is played at lift-off, at the pad, at a distance-attenuated volume."
  ],
  "fireworks.boom": {
    "subtitle": "subtitles.fireworkshaders.boom",
    "sounds": [{"name": "fireworks/boom", "stream": false}]
  },
